{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1525483-candlelight-city-shard","id":1525483,"title":"Candlelight City [Shard]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-15T15:02:10-08:00","id":1525483,"title":"Candlelight City [Shard]","content":"The CofD generally exists somewhere between the microcosms and the macrocosms- from one end, the characters deal with the local threats and challenges, from the other all kinds of intricate regional and global powers shape and clash across their territory. Generally, this is represented through the Tier system, moving all the way from local to cosmic, with Hunter basically establishing those concepts and solidifying it through the different orgs that compose the setting. However, lately I have a thought rattling through my head about shaking this concept up a bit- instead of weaving the global and the local together, let's fold them upon one another. Let's have a single, local setting, which is self contained yet has all of the moving pieces inside of it.<br /> <br /> Let's have the Candlelight City.<br /> <br /> Basically, the Candlelight City represents a generic, Hunter focused Mega City or a metropolitan area- something which is place which has enough people, businesses and organizations to be able to carry the weight of the setting as a whole yet local enough for the characters to be able to get from one edge of the city to the other in a relative short time, if they are using a taxi. The exact size of the city is less important, obviously- it should just be &quot;as large as needed&quot;, yet &quot;basically its own thing&quot;. In this Shard, Tiers still have a role, yet with a twist- instead of going <i>wide</i> they go <i>deep</i>. Tier 1 represents the City's surface level- some strange things which bump in the night, some strange mysteries or threats the affect the character's life, some basic fighting between hunters and monsters who need to cover their tracks. Tier 2, however, represent something which is much more constant- those are gangs, stores, small businesses and social movements that are shifting with the City's atmosphere yet very much colour and define it- the common hunter hears about them and potentially stumble upon them on a daily basis, while many still offer services to the general public. They represent much more complex threats as well, where numerous monsters work together or try to influence numerous people at once. Tier 3 basically represent the pillars of the City- those orgs might as well have built the City: the Mayor is funded by them, they hold key positions in the local government, they have signs and billboards screaming their names- yet at the same time, they are mysteries buried deep under the City's surface. Rumors about them are whispered all across the City, yet no one knows what's true and what's false- other than the orgs themselves, obviously. Monsters who work at that scale corrupt the whole local government, holding assets of interest and fund projects which could endanger millions. And what about Tier 4, you ask? This is far beyond the scope of mortals. This is the City itself- the very foundations upon which it is built, and which hold secrets that could shatter the human soul.<br /> <br /> So with that in mind, let's see how well we adapt the different orgs into the City setting, shall we?<br /> <br /> <b><u>Tier 2</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Ashwood Abbey:</b> join the Ashwood Abbey- the coolest club in town and a place well known for its debaucheries. There were numerous complaints and protests against the club throughout the years, with its name being connected to a number of scandals as some among the richest and most influential people were seen going through its blacken doors. This is probably why even after the different allegations about the club's distribution of drugs, wild sexual parties and occasional dead people found on the alley behind them at the end of the night, they managed to avoid being closed. Entering the Ashwood Abbey, however, is not cheap: you either pay the entrance fees or you don't get in (unless you get an invitation), and even if you can get in, not everyone has the same access. Those who pay for the basic level enjoy music, drinks, dance and whatever decadence their mind can conjure. Those who pay for the gold card, however, get special treatments, massages, private rooms and so forth. There are also rumors about the so called &quot;black card&quot;- and those who manage to pay for it are said to enjoy a &quot;experience of a lifetime&quot;. <br /> <br /> <b>Long Night:</b> the local evangelical Church is viewed as somewhat radical in the eyes of most of the City's denizens. The so called Long Night Church is very vocal and well known for its intimidating congregations. Their followers go around the City's streets, warning that the End if Nigh and that the Rapture is upon us. Most people ignore them, but they do have groups of loyal followers, all of which believe that they must be warry of sin and prepare for the coming End of Times. As their followers go from door to door in an attempt to bring more stray souls to the embrace of the Lord, the leaders of the congregation work more actively to prepare to the coming Apocalypse. They gather weapons, food, and prepare shelters for the coming war against the Devil's armies- for they know that not all of their followers, if any, will escape the terror through the Rapture. In fact, the war has already begun- there are demons around walking in humans bodies, which must be slain in the name of the Lord, for only after their death the Christ would come and bring salvation upon the world... or whatever would remain of it.<br /> <br /> <b>Loyalists of Thule:</b> the Schulz family is among the university's greatest donors- for years, their scions went to study there in the faculty of history, and the building itself is named after them. Somewhat ironically, however, the family does not like to discuss its own personal story- how the now cursed patriarch of the family was a very close associate of Himmler, especially in the search after the mystical, pre-human civilization of Thule. While the family have constantly tried to repent for the sons of its bloodline, the taint has stuck and they have left Germany with their valuables and immigrated to the US, where they donate most of their money to fight racism and fascism alongside maintaining historical integrity. That's at least, on what their expenses are written upon. In truth, the Schulz also use their money on their own, secret society- the Loyalists of Thule. As it seems, their patriarch haven't only tried to find Thule- he succeed. There were monsters introduced to the Nazi regime thanks to his help, and he provided occult secrets which allowed a much greater disaster and suffering within an already horrible event. The Schulz moved to the Us to escape their past- but the hunt it down, for many of those monstrosities have left to America after the war, and in order to pay for the debt burned upon them by their bloodline, it is the duty of the Loyalists to put an end for the horrors of their past.<br /> <br /> <b>Network 0:</b> most people don't notice it- the QR code found on flyers, hanged near graffities, slipped into the email box. It is always accompanies with &quot;SEE THE TRUTH&quot; and the initials N0. For the average person, this is just a spam, most likely a link leading you to some fishing scheme or drug selling Telegram group. The truth, however, is much stranger- those who scan the code are lead to a &quot;human verification page&quot;, including all kinds of strange quizzes, mazes and tiresome verification methods. Most people get bored midway and leave. Some, however, persist, reaching the final page stating &quot;ARE YOU READY FOR THE TRUTH?&quot;. Those who click &quot;yes&quot; are lead to a secret link to a app called Network 0. By downloading it, the person gets access to a new, underground social media, one which discuss the rumors and anomalies that happen in the city. No payment is required- the truth is free for use, after all. All that is expected is that those who are members would share their own information in the platform. The darkness must be exposed, and those with access to the Network will be the first to see it.<br /> <br /> <b>Nine Stars:</b> look, tons of shit happens in the world. The City is one of the largest human settlements in the world, which only means that a lot of bad shit is going to accompany it. Murders, rapes, torture- everything the wicked mind can conjure will take place in it. When that shit is done by humans, then at least the police can get involved and bring those foul criminals to justice. The problem is when those actions are done by inhuman monstrosities. After all, it is not like monsters are registered citizens, and even if they are how are you going to proof to the judge that they brainwashed a person to jump themselves off the roof with just a glance? A lot of shit goes unpunished, and a lot of cops get very pissed that there is nothing they can do. That's how the Nine Stars were founded- they are those policemen and women who had enough, and decided that those horrors who can't be punished by the law will not be allowed to go unpunished. Sure, that means unauthorized use of weapons, misuse of police budgets and constant need in meddling in reports - all of which paints the group as not too different from corrupted police force and could very well send them all to jail - but justice must be done, even if they skies are to fall. After all, who is to say that the police itself is not corrupted by monsters?<br /> <br /> <b>Null Mysteriis:</b> working within the academy, the association known as Null Mysteriis is an interdisciplinary collective of scientists and researchers of all STEM fields: chemistry, biology, physics, engineering and so forth. On the surface, the organization works to advance cooperation between fields and expose the scientific mysteries and how they could be applied to day to day life. In truth, the association use its budget to investigate the phenomenal world of paranatural beings (or as commoners call them, &quot;monsters&quot;). The group works to both present the results of their research and new discoveries as well as cover on each other ion terms of using their funds as part of their true goal. The city is filled with paranatural beings, after all- a whole new scientific field which just stands empty. One day, when the public will be ready, they will publish their results, showing the world the truth that's hidden beneath the surface. Until then, they are fine with arguing over cookies about whether string theory provides explanation to werewolf shapeshifting or not.<br /> <br /> <b>SWORN:</b> the City is old- but the land is older. There were people there, once, who had their own stories and their own traditions, ones which were wiped out by the ancestors of those who founded the City on their lands. The stories are gone now- but the monsters they warn against have remained, and without those warnings they roam free, devouring innocent lives and festering within the City like a wound. That's where SWORN comes in: the descendants of the indigenous people, SWORN serves both as a protest movement meant to fight against racism and systematic discrimination against them as well as gathering the remnants of their ancestors' knowledge, seeking to piece together how they once fought against the monsters. As such, SWORN fight both human and inhuman threats to their community, keeping them safe from the dangers of the shadows as they rebuild the cultures which were lost to colonialism.<br /> <br /> <b>Union:</b> you don't mess with the worker unions. Big companies always try to abuse their employees, grinding them down for profit, and they do whatever they can just to make sure that they won't fight back. While unions are meant to deal with predatory companies, the Union recognize that there are other threats to their workers- horrors which actually seek to devour common people who just want to go to work and go back home in one piece. Taking the same tactic used against the hungry corporations, the Union works both as a community guard and as a political entity- the fight against the lone monsters who prey on those who walk alone in the dark and fight against the institutions controlled by dark monsters who try to enslave humans for their own foul goals. In a place as large as the City, it is easy for those monsters to worm inside and devour a life while most people ignore their screams- and it is up to the Union to maintain the sense of common goal and community in the City, making sure that when someone would call to help there will be someone to answer the call- with a club and a gun in their hands.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So I planned on also covering conspiracies in this post, but it took longer than I expected and time is late here, so I'll try to finish conspiracies by tomorrow. Hope you liked it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T17:58:00-08:00","id":1525488,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll have to read the rest, but the premise gives me cyberpunk-esque vibes. Can\u2019t go wrong with that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T14:08:44-08:00","id":1525537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1525483-candlelight-city-shard?p=1525488#post1525488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ll have to read the rest, but the premise gives me cyberpunk-esque vibes. Can\u2019t go wrong with that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. And nothing says that a person can't reskin CoD into something else entirely (like, say, Sci-Fi Near-Future Cyberpunk) if they want to!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T16:05:29-08:00","id":1525549,"title":"","content":"I like it. Slashers could serve as a decent basis for cyber psychos if you go the full cyberpunk route. But I dont think this really has to lean cyberpunk either, it could just as easily be full Gotham.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-17T03:28:29-08:00","id":1525560,"title":"","content":"So while Tier 2 orgs generally didn't require much adaptation to the City (which makes sense, considering their different scale), let's now move to the more interesting case of conspiracies, shall we?<br /> <br /> <b>Aegis Kai Doru:</b> the City's museum of history is well known for its comprehensive collection of relics and artifacts across many different cultures. Much of the museum's budget is dedicated towards expanding its collection, making different exhibitions to educate the next generation and present newcomers the wonders of the world (even though many complain about the legality of the methods in which those items are being procured). While the museum is supported by the City, it is in fact being maintained by a small family of Greek descent, who deal with both the required PR and the additions of new relics to the collection. Like all museums, the City's museum is also not fully opened to the public, maintaining a large archive who is claimed to deal with the more &quot;delicate&quot; items. According to the rumors, however, the museum's archive is much more than a &quot;research only area&quot;- there is a vast labyrinth beneath the structure, they claim, one which predates the museum, if not the City. The museum itself is merely a cover up, maintained by its sponsors as part of their sacred missions to collect relics of occult nature- and little will stand in their way to acquire new relics from those they deem unworthy to hold, which is anyone but themselves, protecting them with a Shield and Spear.<br /> <br /> <b>Ascending Ones:</b> the criminal underground of the City is complex and widespread, yet one of the great powers controlling it is a collection of gangs and traffickers known as the Ascending Ones. Everything you need, the Ascending Ones can get- drugs, weapons, occult reagents and more. Everything can be bought and sold- for a price. Most people in the City try to avoid places claimed by the Ascending Ones, even though that many hunters turn to them in search for information and armory in their fight against the supernatural. As such, most people who hear about the Ascending Ones merely know them as the force which dominant drug traffic in the City- yet this is merely one of the many layers that the organization maintains. Sometimes, the agents of the Ascending Ones see a potential hidden in a certain costumer, offering them to join them &quot;in prayer&quot;. Those who do discover that the Ascending Ones are not mere criminals- they are a cult, dedicated for seeking unity with God as they combine variety of drugs and poisons in their attempt to &quot;Ascend&quot;. Those who want to leave discover that it is too late for them- the secrets of the Ascending Ones must be protected, and their combinations of drugs and poisons allows them a rigid control over their followers, for only their alchemical secrets can offer protection from them.<br /> <br /> <b>Cheiron:</b> the St Cheiron Hospital is a private institute, well known for its advanced medical technology and high success rate at saving their patients from even the most terrible of conditions- as long as they have the money to pay for it. It is said that the institute has connections with the top pharmaceutical companies in the market, and that they maintain their own R&amp;D facilities, developing new treatments which are later patented and archived. Their greatest advancements are in the field of organ transplant, maintaining a high percent of successful operations and hiring the best doctors that universities has to offer. The hospital, however, is not fully driven by profit- they also do charity, both for tax and PR reasons. However, some whisper that there is a catch in those &quot;donations&quot;- that many times, they are accompanied by contracts which give the hospital control over the body of the patient, or that they simply &quot;lease&quot; them the organs, or that they take part in strange experiments that violate the body and soul of the patient. All of those are, obviously, dirty lies, and the hospital will sue anyone who dares to claim them, as well as trying to claim that the reason that the hospital's management does not reveal itself to the public is because they have some dirty secrets to hide, or that they are part of some satanic conspiracy. They even offer their services for hunters- stitching their wounds, treating their diseases, putting monster claws in their hands, transplanting hives into their brains. Their doctors are very skilled surgeons, after all, and it will be a waste to let good old organs to rot away, regardless of their origin.<br /> <br /> <b>Council of Bones:</b> there are many rumors about the City's graveyard- it is haunted, it is said. It maintains a gateway to the Underworld. It is guarded by a cult dedicated to the dead. All of those rumors are true. The graveyard is found right next to the university, claimed to be so due to the symbolism of maintaining knowledge after death. The transition between the university and the graveyard is almost nonexistent- there are no fences or walls, no signs or blockades. The road just flows into the garden, and before one might notice they are surrounded by graves. This makes the work of the Council of Bones much easier- the self proclaimed Chosen of Death, they are composed of scholars who seek to understand the true nature of ghosts and the undead. The vast majority of their members are found among the university's faculty staff, claiming to maintain an ancient bargain with Death itself from generation to generation meant to serve the dead and protect the living. Only those who are found of sufficient passion to the mysteries of Death are initiated to the cult, and only after trials meant to verify whether an individual ahs an affinity to the Beyond, and if their intentions are indeed pure. Those found to be abusing their gifts are all too welcomed to serve Death after their own demise, after all.\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Lucifuge:</b> one of the oldest and richest families in the City, the Luciani are surrounded by mystery and whispers. It is said that they are the main funders of the current mayor, putting him in their debt and controlling his every action. That the matriarch of the family have lived for centuries, ever since that the City was founded, and that the family covers it us using false identities and fake names. That family have gained its wealth through bargains with the Devil, and that they still make sacrifices to demonic forces. The Luciani, themselves, rarely get involved with the general public, keeping their distance from the masses and barely even discussing with people from their own social circles, adding fire to the rumors surrounding them. Regardless of the rumors, the Luciani are treated as a noble family, and they keep their bloodline well supervised, leaning towards arranged marriages as the family document its complex genealogy. According to some leaked documents, those family trees go deep- all the way to the depths of Hell. Documents featuring Lucifer as the progenitor of the family line circle among conspiracy theories, as well as pictures of certain Luciani members fighting demonic entities, or possibly summoning them? The context is unclear, but if the rumors are true, the family seems to use a different name for themselves among their members and allies. The Lucifuge- those who escaped the Light.<br /> <br /> <b>Malleus Maleficarum:</b> charismatic and handsome, Father Baudolino is the leader of the local catholic congregation in the City. Living in the St Longinus Church, he guides the community with beautiful sermons and gentle care. The Church itself is being cared by a small staff of nuns and priests, all are fully devoted to Baudolino and handpicked by him directly. Little is known, however, that the staff is not merely being trained in theology and care for the poor- each is chosen for their past skills in hand to hand battle, guns and other forms of attack. The City is a dangerous place, after all, and there is always danger to the faithful. The Church itself is being built like a fortress- high walls, spiked fences, locks everywhere... it even has an underground catacombs that according to the rumors is filled with weapons, food, and strange coffins who are bound in iron. The statues of gargoyles and angels watch from the Church's walls, threatening any coming danger, and the pictures of the saints guards the faithful within their walls, seeking any sign of corruption. The Church is basically God's bastion, prepared for war, and if the rumors are being told the priests are fully armed themselves, waging war against heretical horrors under the name of the Hammer of Witches all across the City, all in the name of God.<br /> <br /> <b>Task Force: VALKYRIE:</b> a lot of strange shit is going around in the City, so it is a little wonder that the government have noticed the constant supernatural activity and have decided to deal with it. Formed to monitor, control and cover up the supernatural, Task Force: VALKYRIE's commanding base sits in a ghost building in the edges of the City- at least, that's what the rumors claim. According to the same rumors, those governmental agents care less about protecting innocent lives and more about regulating the status quo, making sure that the truth won't get out and that chaos will not rise. Their agents all work in some straw company called Midgard Inc, which serves as their cover (Midgard officially deny those claims and have plenty of proofs that they are, indeed, a real consulting company with numerous clients, the mayor included). They never act without orders, even though they themselves don't know who their superiors are and what goals they have- only that they must to keep the charade that the supernatural does not exist. That means not only hunting down those supernatural who cause mayhem and draw attention, but also turning against hunters who are not careful in their job or that try to get the truth out. Still, this is just a rumor, nothing more- that is, until you see agents in black holding weapons made through impossible technology. Then, you better run before you too will become part of the rumors.<br /> <br /> <b>VASCU:</b> composed out of former special services agents and detectives who served in the police, the Vanguard Serial Crimes Unit is a team of private investigators meant to solve those crimes which law enforcement generally can't reach. There is so much crime in the City, after all, and so little budget to the police, that the authorities simply can't be everywhere all at once, allowing groups such as VASCU to grow- they collect the evidence, find the suspects, track down their victims and build the case, handing it over to the authorities all wrapped up nicely. As private investigators, while VASCU is often employed by private citizens who don't have their wrongs solved by the system, the company must still abide by law, getting proper authorizations when tracking down a suspect and avoiding violence when not in self defense. As most of the unsolved cases are generally being related to monsters, it is a little wonder that VASCU deals mostly with those threats, all of which makes it extremely difficult to build a proper case. Still, VASCU seems to have a pretty high success rate. Nobody known for certain, but the rumor claims that VASCU are not mere special security agents- that they are a product of an experiment, conducted in the City during the Cold War. One which was deemed as a failure and then dismantled, unaware that it did succeeded due to the lab rats hiding their own capabilities. That each of them is an awakened psychic, going through a special treatment called the Wintergreen Process, which awakens those predictive and calculative abilities through mental trauma. That they hunt criminals not because they want to, but because they are designed to do so, and ignoring the feedback will drive them mad. Whether true or not, VASCU are quite good at their job- even though that law breaking hunters are not immune from becoming their targets when a victim files a complain against them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Aaaand that's it for the core conspiracies! Let me know what you are thinking while I consider the other orgs in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-17T15:57:23-08:00","id":1525574,"title":"","content":"Ok, so let's talk a bit about the Witch Finder orgs, shall we?<br /> <br /> <b>Division Six:</b> in a place as crowded with mysteries and supernatural influences as the City, it is a little wonder that it has its fair share of conspiracy theorists. Originally a group of hunters who stumbled upon what they claimed to be &quot;reality deviants&quot;, those hunters have clearly caught on something. A few days after researching some occult infrastructure, a person named Mr. Jones have came to them and presented himself as a representative of a local agency meant to deal with those threats. Complimenting them for their dedication and skills, he told them that the government have decided to recruit their services to fight reality deviants, something which the group have happily agreed upon. As part of their recruitment, each member went through a special process meant to &quot;strength their minds against brainwashing&quot;, and they were granted guns and resources, as well as some of Mr. Jones's contacts. Now, Division Six serves the country in protection from monsters. Task Force: VALKYRIE have recently found out about the group, something which have caused some questions to rise- Task Force: VALKYRIE have never heard on this so-called &quot;Division Six&quot;, and as far as they are aware, they are the only ones assembled by the government to deal with supernatural threats in the City. Still, rivalry between secret service agencies is not unheard of, and so VALKYRIE currently only keeps a close watch, all while trying to find out who &quot;Mt Jones&quot; actually is.<br /> <br /> <b>Keepers of the Source:</b> the world is dying, and someone has to save it. The Keepers of the Source have started as a peaceful local protest movement in the City, rising against the rapid industrialization of the City which brought air pollution, greenhouse gasses and chemical spills. While initially focusing on demonstrations and strikes, the local government found it way too easy to ignore them, which caused their members to grow more and more aggressive. Some members have even claimed to feel the pain of the planet in their flesh, its screams filling their ears as it got abused by humanity. Things became worse when, in attempt to track down the source of the pain, the Keepers were lead to a gathering of monstrous entities who drained the lifeblood of Mother Earth in the middle of the Central Park. This was too much for them to handle- not only humanity defiles the land, but monsters destroy its spirit as well? While the Keepers have maintained their fight against pollution, they have also found a target in monsters, as they drain the Earth and spread their Taint, forming foul Nests all across the City's sacred places. Yet as many monsters have wormed their way to the high ranks in both the local government and industry, many Keepers have started practicing eco-terrorism, and lately most no longer differentiate between monster held assets and human held ones.<br /> <br /> <b>Promethean Brotherhood:</b> the museum of natural history contains many precious artifacts, and as such the management makes sure to maintain the best security that money can have. It is not to say, however, that break ins never happen. A few years ago, a person called Jacob Hite have walked through the museum's latest exhibition about Greek culture, when one of the items drew his attention- a large marble tablet, covered in scripture in some unknown language. While he couldn't understand the writing, something in the tablet called him, almost making him understand through the figures on it its secret meaning- power through sacrifice. When asked about the tablet, the guide quickly claimed that the tablet was put out by accident, and that it should be moved to the archive due to the lack of information about it. Jacob couldn't have let it happen. Later that night, there was a break to the museum, and the tablet was stolen- finding its way to Jacob's basement. Covering his tracks behind, Jacob have researched the tablet for years, getting in touch with experts who knew how to keep their mouth shot. Eventually, they unlocked its secrets- a ancient ritual called the Rite of Hecate, where through a special sacrifice one could still the power of a monster. As this point, Jacob's basement looked more like an Orphic temple than anything else, and he and his coworkers have started their hunt in order to test and perfect the Rite. Now, the Promethean Brotherhood is a secret society led by Jacob's son (the Rite has its cost, and Jacob made one too many mistakes to get out of its alive), all dedicated for powering themselves with stolen power- yet by doing so, they gained their fair share of enemies. At the top of the list, however, are the powers behind the museum- the Brotherhood had to burn down their own base more then once as the Aegis Kai Doru planned to raid it. The tablet is theirs after all- and they want it back.<br /> <br /> <b>Knights of St George:</b> Hosting a diverse and heterogenic society, the City has a small population of Anglicans within its borders. Those followers generally gather in the Church of St George, which is well known for its symbolism of the knight slaying the dragon. The Church itself is pretty simplistic is design, with modest design that almost blends in the background. Its congregation is not too devoted, generally gathering during Sundays and on special events only. As such, most of the time the Church stands empty, hosting only its few priests and most devoted congregation members. That doesn't stop the rumors from spreading, however. According to those whispers, the reason that the Church is being maintained even though its own community lacks interest in its existence is that beneath it, there is a bound demon, one bearing a draconic visage. That the Church itself serves as its seal, keeping it dormant under the power of prayers and sacred ceremonies. That the members of the Church are not some innocent priests- they are all trained in weaponry and martial arts, wearing armors and bearing arms as if they were the knights of old. That the leader of the Church is, in fact, a self proclaimed royal descendant- sometimes, even said to be of a bastard line to Richard the Lionheart himself! Worse, the rumors claim that those secret &quot;Knights of St George&quot; gather in the Church and practice their secret ceremonies not to merely keep the dragon asleep, but to drain its power. That they augment their dreams with the songs of the bound demon, deriving their own demons from their own souls. That they summon those demonic beings in their service- and that they seek out those who try to awaken the dragon from its sleep and slay them, for the wakening of the dragon might destroy the whole city, if not the whole world. And then, after thinking on all of those rumors, one would look on the modest, almost blank building, laugh it out and move on their way. There is no way something so devious hides beneath such a plain surface, after all. One would need to be a extraordinary liar to pull something like that off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T09:50:49-08:00","id":1525595,"title":"","content":"So let's move to our next batch of orgs- the Spirit Slayers, shall we?<br /> <br /> <b>Bear Lodge:</b> the City is a overcrowded, stressed place- countless people go through it, interact, trade, scream, murder, all day long seven days a week. It is little wonder that from time to time, people need to take a break. The most popular resort location is the Forest- a few hours drive, where many lodges and tourist spots are ready for those who want a vacation, taking some time off and being one with nature. While there are many activities for those who go to the Forest, such as tracks, spas and guided tours, one of the more popular activities in those resorts in hunting- and the Forest itself is filled with all kinds of beasts, be them wolves, boars, deer, bears or some other, less natural variety. Among the many resorts dedicated for hunting activity, the Bear Lodge is the most prestigious and well known. The Lodge is staffed all year long, providing guidelines about which animals are allowed to be hunted and at which period- as well as some &quot;special&quot; targets, meant for those regular clients who have shown both potential and interest in the highest quality kind of prey. The Lodge will supply those hunters with whatever they need, be them weapons, traps or lures, and would pay handsomely for such captured prey as well as adding the name of the hunter to their Hall of Fame- yet once you leave the Lodge's bounds, you are on your own. The Lodge will not lend their help to those who went hunting unprepared- those who disrespect nature should pay their dues, after all.<br /> <br /> <b>Illuminated Brotherhood:</b> the life in the City's university are wild- there are parties, alcohol, sex and all kinds of drugs waiting for students who seek to have fun throughout the semester. As such, those who supply the best pills are generally the ones who get the cash- and perhaps not surprisingly, the ones who have their hands on the supply chain are not some devious traffickers or the popular kids, but the nerds of chemistry classes. The Illuminated Brotherhood was founded a few years ago, as a group of students have mixed the wrong types of chemicals and accidently produced a strange drug that allowed them to interact with beings beyond the mortal realm. Originally thought to be some sort of hallucinations, the group have focused on researching and refining the chemicals responsible for the experience, and soon after have came on the idea to market those drugs during parties. The product was a huge success, even though a few students have wen through strange episodes or got themselves unalived in strange circumstances, but everything was covered up while the Brotherhood kept trying to understand the secrets behind the chemicals. While they have managed to evade law enforcement with little repercussions, lately a different player have been drawn to them- the Ascending Ones do not like when others try to walk into their territory, and the popularity of their &quot;spirit drugs&quot; means less sales for the more traditional products- not to mention the whole spiritual possessions they need to deal with.<br /> <br /> <b>Talbot Group:</b> all parents love their children- it is both their duty and nature. However, sometimes your children don't grow up to what you wanted them to be. Sometimes it is small things, like going to study arts instead of sciences in high school. Sometimes, it is something more significant- their behavior changes, they keep secrets from you, they hang out with the wrong kinds of crowds, and do things you certainly don't approve of. Let them to do what they see fit, and it is likely things will swirl out of control, and before you'll notice your precious child will be lost to the darkness- they would become a monster. But worry not! The Talbot Group is here to save them! This private institute excels at fixing wrong kinds of behaviors and calibrating young souls before it will be too late. No matter what the cause is, Talbot are there to make sure that your children will grow up to be functional, operating, humans. The lightest cases could be solved easily in the three months Summer Camp in the Woods. The harder ones will require the year long therapy session in a special facility hosted by the Talbot Group. All of the Talbot Group's staff is made of qualified psychologists and lifestyle trainers, but more importantly, they are all parents, who have all went through the same process as you did, either losing their children to monstrosity or saving them through the Group's many programs. So don't you worry- you can trust the Talbot Group. All parents love their children- even if they don't understand it.<br /> <br /> <b>Les Mysteres:</b> The Association of Mystics and Mediums, commonly better known as Less Mysteres, is a legal union which connects the many practitioners of crystal weaving, voodoo, mediumship and all other methods by which mystics use to heal, guide and read the fortunes of their clients. Originally founded by a famous Voodoo Queen, Les Mysteres has started originally as a loose organization where practitioners of different traditions have united together both in order to expel charlatans and those who abuse their community and with strange spiritual threats that often plague the people in the City. As the City grew in power, more and more mystics have joined Les Mysteres, turning it into an actual regulatory body which allows enough freedom for individual mediums to practice their art yet still makes sure that they don't create bad reputation to the genre as a whole. While most people generally either view the Mysteres as self deluded or come for them only to have their fortunes read and gain spiritual advices and boons, the organization has a secret, more important mission- the gods of the land have long been without people to speak in their name, and with the City rapidly growing and evolving the divine realms are left without tributes and offerings, causing them to act madly and exact vengeance as they lose their own identity within the chaos. The Mysteres, in return, were the ones to rise to commune with the gods, bargaining with them over the souls of the possessed and fighting against those monsters who seek to either abuse their gifts or disrupt the ancient rituals which are meant to keep them satisfied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T03:57:47-08:00","id":1525630,"title":"","content":"Moving on to the next Hunter supplement: Night Stalkers-<br /> <br /> <b>Barrette Commission:</b> the City has its own upper echelons of power- and there are always people who seek to abuse it. Monsters have put it a target for themselves to worm to worm their way to the top brass, seeking to abuse the people of the City on a collective scale for their own, dark intentions. Someone has to protect the people- and that someone is the Barrette Commission. That powerful lobby of local politicians have one goal before their eyes: to make sure that if someone manipulates the goals of the government, it would be humans. For years they have managed to make sure that no monster would take the office of the mayor, and mostly keep their close environment from monstrous &quot;advisors&quot;. Still, the monsters don't give up easily, and have their own lobbies to try and push for their own goals, creating an intricate power struggle where the Commission probably has the most information about which monsters actually run the City and to what degree, yet they keep that information secret as a way to blackmail their enemies. While some members of the Commission do care about the people they represent, many care merely about preserving their own power- yet overall, they are doing a pretty good job. Too good, actually- for some reason, their interests seems to often conflict with the commands which VALKYRIE gains from its commandments, putting the two groups at odds with one another, and who knows how that conflict might end up as.<br /> <br /> <b>Maiden's Blood Sisterhood:</b> the university in the City is a wild please, where many people have their vulnerabilities exposed- and there are those who are waiting to exploit those vulnerabilities, especially in the case of young women. This is where the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood comes in. One of the oldest sororities in the university, the Sisterhood is dedicated for protecting its members and other women from the monsters who use the university's social life to lure victims to their doom. They mostly focus on prevention, teaching their members how to read the signs, notice the tells and avoid suspicions figures, as well as reporting them to the Sisterhood directly. But when a predator falls under their radar, they are quick to act, isolating the figure and bringing it down. Due to their high status in the campus and long survival time, the Sisterhood have produced a number of high status members that support the sorority from outside the university, as well as learned a few tricks in witchcraft by using a feminist theological tradition that helps them in their hunt. That inclusion of witches among their members have made some hunters to view the Sisterhood in a very negative light, all while they themselves hold the Illuminated Brotherhood in contempt due to the drugs which they carelessly sell that give monsters more vulnerabilities to exploit.<br /> <br /> <b>Night Watch:</b> each city has its slums, and the City is no different. Being one of the largest metropoli in the world, it draws many immigrants from both within the country and all around the world, many of which are left to rot in its poorer districts as they are unable to find a job and integrate. The City leaves behind those who can't fend for themselves, allowing crime to grow and creating victims to those who seek to prey upon the weak. The Night Watch, however, stands vigilant against those horrors. Rising from among the poor and weak, the Watch serves as some sort of a community guard meant to fill the void left by the police and other law enforcement forces. After all, those who live in the slums don't have a way to demand their rights, and it's easy for the City to turn a blind eye and focus on its own growth and success while the weak are being left behind. Generally, the Night Watch performs patrols across the slums, keeping a eye open for those who are in need and reach out to help in case they find a suspicious figure preying upon innocent bystanders. Sometimes, however, they take a more active approach- rooting out where a certain serial predator nests and making sure that it would never claim any more victims. While they are quit popular in their own area, as they rise in success so they draw an unwanted attention- not many people are so accepting of the idea of armed militia groups, especially among minorities and low social economic status people, and as certain members of the Watch view human threats to their community as not so different from inhuman ones, the police feels the stress to come and get rid of the so called &quot;Night Angels&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Cainite Heresy:</b> the City is not a ordered place. It is a crowded, stressed, violent society, where any semblance of law is only kept due to tight enforcement with low resources. As such, many crimes are left unresolved in the City- leaving conspiracy theorists to try and patch up the disparate instances into a coherent picture, and one of those theories which is meant to explain some of the most violent crimes is the so called &quot;Cainite Heresy Theory&quot;. According to the theory, many of those crimes as not some random actions of madmen- they point towards certain graffities that are left on the crime scene, many of which bear a strange symbol as part of their design, or how surviving witnesses that mention how the assailants have kept screaming &quot;Who is Cain?!&quot; while preforming the horrendous acts, or how all of the related targets are always of shady nature, either shell companies or somehow related to the dark rumors that circle around the City. They claim that the Cainite Heresy is partially a terrorist organization and partially a anarchist group, seeking to free the City from monstrous control. That their members are all brainwashed soldiers chosen among the victims of monsters, taught to seek out vengeance even at the cost of their own life. That those individuals are conspiracy theorists by themselves, who believe that monsters have taken control over the central power structures of the City, and as such they must be toppled down regardless of collateral damage. That they are made of many independent hunters, barely connected together by an entity even they don't know and which provides them the means for their terrorist acts. That they follow a strange, gnostic path that even they don't fully understand, where monsters are the children of the Demiurge and those who be branded as criminals in the name of justice are promised salvation by the true god. That the sources which feeds them information, weapons and rituals are devious being themselves, seeking to bring only doom and ruin to the world. Of course, that's just a conspiracy theory. The City just has so much crime and so many crazy people that those who want to find a pattern will find one. But just in case, you are better to know the correct answer to the question &quot;Who is Cain&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-20T14:19:11-08:00","id":1525696,"title":"","content":"Moving next- Mortal Remains:<br /> <br /> <b>Habibti Ma:</b> the City is a crowded place, filled with strange unsavory people and dark societies. The supernatural is crawling everywhere, with people stumbling upon it carelessly. Without any knowledge about what is the true nature of the darkness, people either view it in a divine manner and start worshipping it, or cloak themselves in it to become objects of worship themselves. Strange philosophies and dark religions develop around those entities, spreading like illness as they exploit the vulnerable and twist their minds to their cause, forming cults where one's life are offered as sacrifice to the darkness. Against all of those myriad of ideologies, faiths and secret societies, the Habibti Ma stands vigilant- founded by an immigrant woman called Eme Amun Hassan, she have seen first and the horrors that lurks in those societies, as her son was lured to one from which he never returned. Since then, Habibti Ma operates mostly in the slums where the poor and the immigrants are found (who are generally the ones most abused by cults), both warning them against the dangers cults present, offer them alternatives and eventually fighting head on against the twisted societies. Many times, they do so legally, filing lawsuits, taking custodies, exposing to the public the horrors that certain charismatic figures do in the name of their own ego. On other times, they act more directly- breaking into cult bases to save children who are about to be sacrificed, stop mass suicides and reprogram those who were brainwashed by cults. And when push comes to shove, the Habibti Ma will face heads on against those false gods who feast on human misery, invoking their own Lady Justice to pass judgement on those who believe they should not be judged.<br /> <br /> <b>Utopia Now:</b> part startup and part real estate company, Utopia Now is a fast growing local company which takes over the City by storm. Everyone agree that they are estimate to have value in at least 2 million dollars, and their value keeps on growing at each day- yet no one seems to agree on what exactly they are selling. To investors, they present a complicated picture about using their bought properties as fast communication network infrastructures, allowing them to produce a variety of technological wonders by top secret design approaches. There is no need to patent those works, they promise- their apps are secured, their techniques are unsolvable, and their promise is huge. No one is sure what exactly is the use for those products, whatever they may be- but they are definitely going to change the world. After all, their technology is indeed impressive (whatever it may be), and all thing about high speed communication and quickly updated wide variety generalized apps based on artificial generalized intelligence prototypes are definitely going to amount to something. At this point, about 15% of the City's properties are actually being held by Utopia Now, so at the very least if all of their technological mambo jumbo would fail, they at least would have back up, right? Just ignore the rumors about how their properties are generally places surrounded by urban legends and missing people incidents, or how they strip apart strange devices of occult origin from those territories, or how there are stories of them fighting strange, biomechanical horrors that call those places home. Ignore that their apps always have strange glitches in them that sprout words like SAVE ME or GOD IS FALLEN. Ignore that their workers all seem to very idealistic about how they are going to turn the City into a true &quot;utopia&quot;. While we had this conversation, their value just jumped to 3.5 million dollars- don't you want a part of the pie?<br /> <br /> <b>Faithful of Shulpae:</b> the life in the slums are harsh. Signs of neglect are everywhere- crime, drug addicts, homelessness, people waiting in line for scraps of food in soup kitchens. The City, after all, is among the largest cities in the world, and so it is little wonder that people are being left behind, hunger gnawing in their stomachs and despair filling their hearts. There is, however, a way out of it- not all of that capitalism crap, obviously. The poor stay poor. No, this is something else- the rumors say that if you are really starving in the City, they will find you. Strange people, looking old yet feel older. Those people simply present a simple offer- join their faith, and you will never starve again. While those who have more resources may say no, those who are truly hungry will never turn such offer down. The rumor, however, doesn't end here- those are not some evangelistic Christians or something like that. Those people don't even live above the ground- instead, they dwell in the sewers, where they gather in temples much older than the City. In those temples, they celebrate their heretical gods, all in the name of a long forgotten god of the feast. Each of their celebrations is about food, eating is seen as a sacred act or worship- and who is more worthy of worship than their own gods? This is the trick, the rumors say- for in order to join the cult, you must participate in their journey to bring gods back to the temple to be worshipped- and many of those gods look, act and scream all too human. Those who are able to stomach the process in which the divine is being feasted upon not only fill their stomachs, but also said to gain the blessings of their gods, perhaps even becoming immortal. Those who don't... well, nobody noticed their suffer in life. Nobody will also find their bodies in death.<br /> <br /> <b>Knights of St Adrian:</b> the City is a place of crime, and the police is cracking under the stress. They need help- and Howard Investigation Services is happy to help. Those bounty hunters and bail bondsman have only one goal- to make sure that those who are meant to go to trial will get there. Founded by Casey Howard, the company is on a constant watch, sweeping through the City all the way from the slums to the ivory towers, for as long as there is a contract, neither status or money will stop them from filling out their obligations. This alone makes the company into one of the most infamous groups on the City- everyone heard of an instance where their members broke into someone's house and drugged him all the way to the police for something as simple as a driving ticket which wasn't paid, with the people of the slums knowing to hide when they hear their motorcycles roaming across their roads. Yet in the end, this is simply a dirty job that someone needs to do, all meant to maintain the status quo in the City. As such, it is a little wonder that there are many stories who try to paint the company in a negative light- that many times, they don't just follow their police contracts- but that they capture innocent people, kidnapping them in service of some obscure, eldritch power, serving the all mighty dollar above all else. Others say that the story is false- but that the hunting is true. That Howard Investigation Services is merely a cover up for a religious institute known as the Knights of St Adrian- that each of their members is marked as a soldier of God, and that they roam around dragging demons who hide wearing human skin, dragging them all the way back to Hell. That the &quot;God&quot; that they serve is not God at all, but a devil by itself, wearing the face of an angel and feasting upon blood sacrifice. That the &quot;demons&quot; they hunt are indeed just regular entities who try to live their daily life, far from God (or the Devil)'s sight- yet whether their actions are justified or not is of little care to the Knight. A contract is a contract, after all, whether it is made with Man or with God, it must be fulfilled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T13:28:50-08:00","id":1525746,"title":"","content":"Time for the next section- Tooth and Claw:<br /> <br /> <b>The Reckoning:</b> while the largest Protestant congregation in the City belongs to the Long Night, smaller ones still exist. One of the more fringe groups of religious fundamentalists call themselves the Reckoning- following priest Derek Campbell, the group is very loud compared to its size, constantly preaching about the coming Day of Reckoning where &quot;all shall known the fear of God&quot;. In truth, the group is practically a cult- in their view, God reveals itself through fear, and as monsters instigate pure dread unlike any other they are by themselves objects of worship. As such, the congregation commonly seeks out after monsters, trying to pursue them to join their prayers so they could experience the divine through them. The problem comes, however, is that not all monsters are equal- some are more human than the others, and every monster has it enemies, and generally the more human ones ends up hunting the monstrous ones. As those monsters who have strayed from their humanity (or where never human in the first place) are the ones which inspire the most refined horror, the cult ends protecting the worst of those monsters from the ones who seek to free the world from their presence- be them other monsters, hunters, or both. As such, as charismatic as Derek might be, his cult grows the ire of the rest of the Vigilant community which would end up deciding that enough is enough. Derek, obviously, has a plan- new cults can be started, and he already have a number of stolen identities prepared. In case of crises, he would only need to tie some loose ends, and to the darkness he'll go...<br /> <br /> <b>Yuri's Group:</b> the Vigil is a ever taxing process, where people put their body and soul on the line, making tremendous sacrifices for which they'll never be thanked for. Hunters are, by their very basis, unsung heroes, and as they experience more and more horrors they are more likely to get detach from the world, eventually snapping and becoming their own worst nightmare. That's where the Yuri's Group comes in. Everyone needs a place where they can confess their guilts, shames and regrets, places where they will be accepted and not be judged. The support circles of the therapy group are meant to answer that call- hunters from all across the city gather and share their stories, learning how to come in terms with their failures and how to live with the horrors that they have witnessed. Managed by licensed therapists, while there weren't originally many hunters willing to expose their pain in front of strangers, eventually more and more hunters were drawn to its facilities, seeking and finding solace behind closed doors where they will not be judged. Ever since their founding, the number of hunters who go through episodes of extreme violence or fall to self harm has slowed down, showing that the Group's therapists apparently know what they are doing. However, lately it has been discovered that certain therapy circles are not meant to support hunters- but monsters. While the official statement is that it is meant to help them maintain their own humanity, this paints the whole organization as untrustworthy, causing hunters to drop out out of the fear that their secrets will be discovered by those who would abuse them. Perhaps it is better to wait a bit before starting the mixed circle sessions, ha?<br /> <br /> <b>Merrick Institution:</b> the Merrick Institution for Gifted Children was pretty infamous all across the City. While using a fancy title to describe itself, it was, in truth, known to be a &quot;educational facility&quot; into which parents through children they either couldn't raise, or that were viewed as too &quot;problematic&quot; to deal with. Many children were sent to the Institute in order to &quot;correct&quot; them, and while it was always proud of its successes, almost everyone knew that entering Merrick is the same as entering an asylum- many would enter, few would get out. A year ago, however, a fire broke in the facility, burning it to the ground. There were no survivors- all documentation was burned, all staff members were killed, all patients were proclaimed dead. Nothing was left behind. The company who managed the facility declared bankruptcy after being sued for crucial safety issues which caused the fire. A settlement was made between the owners and the families of the patients under strict NDA, and that was the end of it- at least, that's what most of the public believes in. The rumors, however, tell a very different story- Merrick was not a &quot;educational facility&quot;, neither it was merely a place where parents would dump unwanted children. It was a human experimentation facility, operated by the government to create &quot;super soldiers&quot; by conditioning children and probing their bodies in an attempt to awaken some &quot;latent psychic abilities&quot;. For years they operated in the shadows, until one day, they messed up- while they did managed to awaken the potential in the abused children, they did not manage to fully condition them. The test subjects rebelled, all safety protocols failed, and in the war the whole place got burned down, leaving Task Force: VALKYRIE to cover the mess up. The children, however, didn't die- they escaped, living now in the streets of the City's slums, building their own communities far from the public eye. They have also managed to salvage numerous files and date about the insidious people behind the institute. Apparently, this project was merely one part of a greater whole- children who &quot;graduated&quot; the Institute are still being abused and employed by the people who operated Merrick, and the goons of the Institute hunt down the children who escaped in order to &quot;close loose ends&quot;. The war is far from over, and when you hear in the news about a unexplained explosion in some company's office or a famous scientist who threw themselves off a window for no reason, know that the children of Merrick are lurking in the shadows, and that they will get their vengeance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T11:16:42-08:00","id":1525801,"title":"","content":"Moving to the last Hunter supplement, let's start with Tending the Fire's compacts, shall we?<br /> <br /> <b>Crimson Halo:</b> like every large city, the City has its own entertainment district- a place where those who seek night's company or a quick rush in exchange for payment can find what they seek. Found between the tourist center and the slums, the district has everything one might desire- escorts, messages, bathhouses, saunas, strip clubs and, obviously, sex workers. Most of the women and men who work into the district are ones which society outright tries to ignore, only using them for whatever they need and throwing them away later- something that the monsters are well aware of, and that are quick to exploit. Standing in their way, however, is the Crimson Halo- the largest brothel (in all but the name) in the district. While the Crimson Halo serves clients for all manners of pleasure as they desire, it is also highly protective of its employee, as the brothel was created by former sex workers who survived through the night and wished to protect other victims from harm in their line of work. As an institute, the Crimson Halo does not focus around monsters specifically- anyone who dares to harm their workers is a fair game, and the institute is well armed with all kinds of protective measures, from security buttons, to knives and guns and up to silver crosses and holy water. While the brothel itself is a fortress which few monsters manage to penetrate, the brothel also offers their protective services to other lone workers need of help, and often patrol through the district to make sure no one is taking more than what they paid for. As the brothel does not differentiate between human and monstrous abusers, they often clash with the more hedonistic and corrupted organizations in the city- the Ashwood Abbey is found in the same district and its patrons often feel entitled when it comes for demanding the services of an escort, while the Hunt Club roams through the streets, clashing against the brothel in their attempts to &quot;get points&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Crossroads Convoy:</b> the City is a large and sprawling metropolitan, drawing people from all across the country and beyond it in search for wealth. Many seek to go to the City, searching for a job or spending their time as tourists, only to return back home in the holidays or travel in the area around the City, such as the Forest. While the City is crowded and filled with violence, the wilderness outside is even more dangerous- there is no law enforcement patrols there, the roads are wide and unsupervised, and many of those who couldn't integrate to the City were pushed to outside its borders, waiting for those who can't easily fend for themselves. In the middle of the night on the wide, empty road, no one will be able to hear you scream. That's where the Crossroads Convoy gets in- starting as a network of smugglers, the Convoy can get anyone to anywhere, and anything from anyplace. Their heart standing in the City, their arms are spread all across the country, holding all kinds of different vehicles and contact people to allow an easy transportation of people and goods from one place to the other. As part of their job, the Convoy also needs to have a few safe routes, as well as making sure that there is no danger lurking on the roads. This makes the Convoy into the most knowledgeable about the horrors that lurk in the wilderness, as well as how to avoid them or, when push comes to shove, fight them.<br /> <br /> <b>Eden Covenant:</b> many people ends up missing in the City every year- with such a crowded population, it is just impossible to track down everyone, so even if foul play was not as common as it is in the City, some people who just drop dead in the wrong place and wrong time would just go unnoticed by the authorities, and their desperate families would have no lead in finding them. Add to this the high crime rate in the City and the constant monstrous involvement, and you'll find that too many people vanish without trace, leaving their loved ones in a grief which could never be resolved. As support group for such people called the Lamplighters was formed- one dedicated for both doing whatever they can to track down missing people, especially in cases of supernatural involvement, as well as giving comfort to those who can't find them, sharing their pain together. Things changed when Ernie Copeland, a local televangelist who have parted ways with the Long Night congregation after he was deemed as &quot;caring more about himself than about God&quot;, have found his way to serve as a support figure in the organization, giving religious comfort to the families. While initially sympathetic and caring, Ernie had other plans in mind- through his religious teachings, he explained that the problem was, first and foremost, with those monsters who stole the identity of their loved ones, or the ones who wear a human guise in order to prey on the trust they gained. That those monsters are sinners both God, and that in order to stop more victims from going missing and leaving their families in tears they must take an active approach and take the fight to the monsters. While the more conservative Lamplighters have tried to stop people from listening to him, it was too little too late- most of the families have started going regularly to Copeland's congregation, and anger does feel better than despair. As the Lamplighters lost control over their own organization, Copeland's actions have started to draw unwanted attention- the Long Night have always kept a watching eye on him, and his violent actions may end up with them taking a more direct approach. The Reckoning, however, are done with waiting- too many of their divine figures fell prey to Copeland's followers, and the City, while large, is too small to contain the ambitions of both Copeland and Campbell.<br /> <br /> <b>Las Guadanas:</b> the criminal underworld of the City is rich, complex, and dangerous. Whether a human or a monster, one should not think they could easily mess with those who call it their home and get out of it in one piece. One of the more dangerous of those organizations is Las Guadanas. Founded by immigrants who settled in the slums, the Scythes are a crime family well known for its uncompromised behavior, violent tendencies and long memories. In many regards, the Guadanas family pretty much runs the slums, dealing mostly with contract killings, human traffic and drug dealing, even though they often clash with the Crossroads Convoy in terms of smuggling and the Ascending Ones in the drug business. No one wants to mess with the Guadanas family, human or otherwise, and the family makes sure to have members of the police force in debt to them, either through bribe or threat. The criminal activity, however, is rumored to cover an even darker side of the family- that at the age of 15, each member of the family is sent to &quot;meet Death&quot;- going through a near death experience, either through drowning, strangulations, poisoning or bleeding out. It is said that those who go through the ceremony have already died, and as such do not need to fear Death again- explaining their unwavering loyalty to the family. According to the rumors, the family is basically a death cult, having its roots all the way from the Aztec Empire and now using their criminal activity as a sacrifice to the old gods of death. Monsters, as those who violate Death (such as the undead and necromancer cults) or harm the family, are often targets of the Scythes- each such enemy is a mark on their walls, and no matter how many generations it would take, they will make sure that they will pay their debt to Death.<br /> <br /> <b>Recalibrators:</b> look, cleaning up is a toiling, dirty, thankless job, but someone needs to do it. Especially in the City- such a violent and angry place obviously makes tons of mess around it. Monsters are killing without trying to cover their tracks, hunters burn down Nests without thinking about an alibi, collateral damage is just been done on left and right. Let this mess spread, and it is only a matter of time before the wrong people will notice the drawn attention, and the wrong people are likely to use it to track hunters down and kill them, join or start cults, trying to become monsters by themselves, blackmail the wrong people or just start a full blown mass hysteria. This is why you need the Recalibrators- a cleaning up service specialized in dealing with the most violent instances. You need to get blood out of the marble? Find a place to bury a body? get the smell of burned offerings out of your hair? The Recalbirators have everything you need. Just keep your mouth shut- the policy is always &quot;no questions asked&quot;. They don't ask how you got to your little situation, you don't ask what they are going to do with the remains or how they know how to deal with the poisonous medusa head. And most important than all- if you hire their services, you keep your mouth shut. You tell no one about that instance, or otherwise you ruiin the cleaning up process. Due to their secrecy and efficiency, the Recalbrators are very popular among the criminal organizations of the City- the Guadanas and the Ascending Ones hire their services frequently, and the St Cheiron hospital have a few constant staff workers in their facilities, while LDI and Deva Corporations both regularly invite their services after they have a &quot;mess up&quot; in their lab. The organization still tries to deal with the leftovers of the Merrick incident, and God the children don't make their life easier as they keep go and burn down more and more laboratories. Even common hunters call for their help in time of need, and they are not above offering their services for monsters- they just need to make sure they keep their mouth shut about it. Hunters who seek after the truth, however, such as Network 0, the Keepers of the Source and the Schulze family, have a much more tense relationship with them, as they try to expose the crimes that the Recalibrators work so hard to hide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}